	(text "TLV320DAC3100 replaces the brief's WM8960 (listed obsolete at Digi-Key). Team approved 2026-11-01.\nRP2354B is I2S master through PIO. The DAC PLL derives its clock from BCLK, so MCLK is not required.\nHeadphones are AC coupled as the datasheet requires; 100 uF is the Adafruit 6309 value. Never ground HPL or HPR.\nAll 3.3 V DAC pins share 3V3_A, then U10 makes DVDD; TI calls the part tolerant of sequencing. R77 holds RESET low while DVDD comes up, per datasheet.\nSPKVDD on 3V3_A meets SPKVDD >= AVDD. Speaker pads J6 are DNP and speaker output is reduced at 3.3 V.\nAIN1, AIN2, GPIO1 unused and left open as on the Adafruit 6309. NC pins 4, 15 per datasheet.\nJack: CTIA wiring. Tip L, Ring1 R, Ring2 GND, Sleeve mic. Mic is biased only if firmware enables MICBIAS.\nHP_DET: with no plug the tip switch connects R78 through R79 to GND (low). A plug opens it (high).\nISOLATION: remove R70-R74, R76 and R75 to use the backup module on J8 without contention."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
